    ],
    "text": "Regulating the Water of Tomorrow:"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000008",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "title",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0011-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "A Multi-Layer Optimization Model for the Great Lakes"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000009",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "heading",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0013-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Summary"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000010",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0004"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0004",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0005"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0013-l0001",
      "p0001-n0013-l0002",
      "p0001-n0013-l0003",
      "p0001-n0013-l0004",
      "p0001-n0013-l0005"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "The Great Lake in the US and Canada faces water problems. The water level of the Great Lake needs to be regulated to satisfy the interests of stakeholders and balance the ecosystem. It\u2019s challenging to control the flow of water due to its complex dynamics. Several organizations have been working on this problem for decades and released solutions such as Plan 2014. However, stakeholders are not satisfied with the current situation and the ever-changing climate has raised uncertainties."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000011",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0001"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0014-l0000",
      "p0001-n0014-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "In this project, a network model of the Great Lakes was built to optimize the water level at any time of the year. It employs a multi-layer modeling design, with both a basic network model for de-"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000012",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "title",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0001-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u5fae\u4fe1\u53f7\uff1aMATHmodels"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000013",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0004"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0014-l0002",
      "p0001-n0014-l0003",
      "p0001-n0014-l0004"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "scribing the major flow processes in the Great Lakes, and an advanced flow model to refine the com- plex factors affecting the flow. Compared with the previous plans, this scheme allows for increased flexibility in lake water levels, accommodating fluctuations between high and low water levels."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000014",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0015-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "The main steps are as follows:"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000015",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0004"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0015-l0001",
      "p0001-n0015-l0002",
      "p0001-n0015-l0003",
      "p0001-n0015-l0004"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "First, a basic network model connecting the five lakes was established to analyze the main water processes. Combined with the analysis of the provided data, several equations were formed to describe the flow of water in the network, which is the foundation of the model. With this model and the dataset, the water level and the flow of water can be calculated."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000016",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0004"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0016-l0000",
      "p0001-n0016-l0001",
      "p0001-n0016-l0002",
      "p0001-n0016-l0003",
      "p0001-n0016-l0004"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Then, an advanced flow model was built based on the basic model to better depict the sophisticated processes affecting the water flow. It is more comprehensive and precise since it analyzes wind, snow, ice jams, and other meteorological factors. This model focuses more on Lake Ontario and the St. Law- rence River to solve the sub-problem. The sensitivity analysis indicated that the model is sensitive to precipitation and less sensitive to the melt of snow."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000017",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0017-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0017-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0017-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0017-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0017-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0017-l0003"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0017-l0000",
      "p0001-n0017-l0001",
      "p0001-n0017-l0002",
      "p0001-n0017-l0003"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "To find a plan that satisfies the stakeholders, multiple benefit and cost functions are first created to form the objective functions, thus creating a multi-objective optimization model. The optimal water level is then solved using the NSGA-II algorithm with operations such as selection, crossover, and mutation."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000018",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0018-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0018-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0018-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0018-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0018-l0000",
      "p0001-n0018-l0001",
      "p0001-n0018-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "In addition, by utilizing data from 2017, the high stability and accuracy of the model are verified in terms of both water use extrapolation based on the multiple linear regression algorithm and compu- tation of the new optimization algorithm."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000019",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0019-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0019-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0019-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0019-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0019-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0019-l0003"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0019-l0000",
      "p0001-n0019-l0001",
      "p0001-n0019-l0002",
      "p0001-n0019-l0003"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "The study succeeded in effectively simulating and optimizing the water level in the Great Lakes by building network models. It's promising, reliable and it's beneficial for all the stakeholders. More importantly, this new plan is also sustainable and will bring the Great Lakes Region towards a better future."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000020",
    "issues": [],
